
A. THE CLASSIFIER — HEARING AND IDENTITY ARE DIFFERENT ANSWERS
  [PASS] A1. an identity answer is confirmed
  [FAIL] A1b. the SPACED and UNSPACED spellings of the same word agree
         "Haanji."
         + actual - expected
         
         + 'unclear'
         - 'confirmed'
         
  [PASS] A2. a denial is denied
  [PASS] A3. a HEARING answer is never an identity answer
  [PASS] A4. a greeting, a question back, or noise is unclear
  [PASS] A6. the natural English confirmations are confirmed (§4.5 F3)
  [PASS] A6b. ...and the denial they contain still wins
  [PASS] A6c. a hearing answer wrapped around one of them is still not an identity answer
  [PASS] A6d. the ambiguous "No, I'm busy." is deliberately UNCHANGED
  [PASS] A7. a positive construction that CONTAINS "no" is not a denial
  [PASS] A7b. ...and every genuine denial still denies
  [PASS] A8. "Right, who's this?" is a question back, not a confirmation
  [PASS] A5. one turn that answers BOTH questions confirms identity

